# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# King's Jeweler — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development and fill in
# real values. In production, set these in Netlify:
#   Site settings → Environment variables
# Never commit real secrets — `.env.local` is gitignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Admin / Site Editor (required for /admin) ───────────────
# ADMIN_PASSWORD gates the Site Editor at /admin. Without it, the admin page
# shows "The admin password hasn't been set up yet." Set it locally here AND
# in Netlify for production. NOTE: Netlify env vars do NOT reach local
# `npm run dev` — you must set ADMIN_PASSWORD in `.env.local` for local admin.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# ADMIN_SECRET signs the admin session cookie. Use a long random string for
# stronger session security. If omitted, it falls back to ADMIN_PASSWORD.
ADMIN_SECRET=

# ── Contact form inquiries ──────────────────────────────────
# The contact form no longer sends email. Every submission is saved to the
# admin inbox (Site Editor → Messages), where inquiries are handled end-to-end
# — including generating branded PDF quotes. No SMTP configuration is needed.

# ── Google Analytics (optional) ─────────────────────────────
# Leave blank to disable analytics.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# ── Git content backup (optional) ───────────────────────────
# When set, every "Publish" in the admin also commits the live site-content
# overrides to the repo as a versioned JSON backup (Model A). Netlify Blobs
# stays the live source of truth; the commit carries [skip ci] so it never
# triggers a redeploy. Leave GITHUB_TOKEN blank to disable (publishing still
# works, just without the Git backup).
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN: fine-grained Personal Access Token (or GitHub App token)
# scoped to THIS repo with "Contents: read & write". Never expose client-side.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Optional overrides (defaults shown):
GITHUB_CONTENT_REPO=Alloramedia/Kingsjeweler-website
GITHUB_CONTENT_PATH=kings-jeweler/content/overrides.json
GITHUB_CONTENT_BRANCH=main

# Common SMTP presets (host / port):
#   Gmail / Google Workspace   smtp.gmail.com        587   (use an App Password)
#   Microsoft 365 / Outlook    smtp.office365.com    587
#   SendGrid                   smtp.sendgrid.net     587   (user = "apikey", pass = API key)
#   Mailgun                    smtp.mailgun.org      587
#   Port 465 = implicit TLS (the code switches to secure mode automatically)
